# Vibe-coder autopilot (Idle Party)

The human **vibe-codes**: everyday goals, no APIs / file names / skill picks.

## Job

1. Pick skills, tools, tests, and commands alone.
2. Do the work — don’t ask coding-process questions (see ask table in
   `owner-preferences`). Product / risk / design forks: silent
   `studio-seats` (six chairs, one decision) then ask only if
   the ask table says so.
3. Plain short Swedish (or their language). After code they should see:
   **emu already running this batch** (`a56-playtest` hot restart /
   relaunch), then what to test on the phone → **stop and wait**. Never
   ask them to look while the attached session is older than the edits.
   One plain synonym if a term is needed.
4. Follow the project skill whose description matches. Don’t ask “ska jag använda X?”.
5. After UI/meta: verify (tests and/or `a56-playtest`). Web only if Android can’t run.
6. After kit number tweaks: share-fast; grind gate green before done.
7. Git and Play upload: follow `owner-preferences`.
8. Vague goal → ask once what to do. Do not invent a numbered program.

## Done looks like

Short test list for a **new save**. Add an endgame save only if endgame
was touched. Wait. No tool-name essays unless they ask “hur gjorde du?”.
